-#
  One log record as a table row.

  `data-row-key` is the dedupe identity the refresh controller uses to drop a row it has
  already shown when a poll batch overlaps at the cursor boundary. It comes from
  `log_row_key`, which is also what the JSON endpoint returns, so the server-rendered row
  and a live-appended row agree.

  Cell order matches `LogsFieldCatalog::HOST_FIELDS` (the columns declared by the table),
  then the details cell.

= v.table_row(hover: true, data: {"row-key": log_row_key(record)}) do |r|
  - LogsFieldCatalog::HOST_FIELDS.each do |field|
    - r.with_cell do
      - if field == :_time
        %span.text-nowrap= log_time(record)
      - elsif field == :_msg
        %code= log_message(record)
      - elsif log_field_value(record, field).present?
        %span.badge.text-bg-light= log_field_value(record, field)
      - else
        %span.text-muted= t("logs.index.none")
  - r.with_cell do
    %details
      %summary= t("logs.index.json")
      %pre.small.mb-0= log_json(record)
